    <briefdescription>
<para>S-pair record for the Franzi boolean Groebner basis algorithm. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Carries the two basis-element indices <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_a174e8c0f0ff85f24f98253a134c085d1_1a174e8c0f0ff85f24f98253a134c085d1" kindref="member">i</ref>, <ref refid="class_pair_a5cc7c357fa4c81c5760aa8e07d68918d_1a5cc7c357fa4c81c5760aa8e07d68918d" kindref="member">j</ref></computeroutput> (a negative <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_a174e8c0f0ff85f24f98253a134c085d1_1a174e8c0f0ff85f24f98253a134c085d1" kindref="member">i</ref> = -k</computeroutput> means the field polynomial <computeroutput>x_k^2 + x_k</computeroutput> is being paired against <computeroutput>F[<ref refid="class_pair_a5cc7c357fa4c81c5760aa8e07d68918d_1a5cc7c357fa4c81c5760aa8e07d68918d" kindref="member">j</ref>]</computeroutput>), the precomputed lead-term <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_affb8bd419fe581fdb84ae0d545fce302_1affb8bd419fe581fdb84ae0d545fce302" kindref="member">lcm</ref></computeroutput>, and a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_a55959c06cfec0d4141a7ddb2f4893354_1a55959c06cfec0d4141a7ddb2f4893354" kindref="member">good</ref></computeroutput> flag set false if either parent has been retired from <computeroutput>F</computeroutput>. Ordered first by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_affb8bd419fe581fdb84ae0d545fce302_1affb8bd419fe581fdb84ae0d545fce302" kindref="member">lcm</ref></computeroutput> (lex), then by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_a5cc7c357fa4c81c5760aa8e07d68918d_1a5cc7c357fa4c81c5760aa8e07d68918d" kindref="member">j</ref></computeroutput>, then by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_pair_a174e8c0f0ff85f24f98253a134c085d1_1a174e8c0f0ff85f24f98253a134c085d1" kindref="member">i</ref></computeroutput>, so the enclosing <computeroutput>std::set&lt;<ref refid="class_pair" kindref="compound">Pair</ref>&gt;</computeroutput> queue pops the smallest pair next. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
